# Keep the build context small. Without this, every build ships the whole ioq3
# submodule, node_modules, and any locally-generated pk3 files to the daemon
# before a single instruction runs. This is a prerequisite for a fast dev loop,
# not cleanup.
#
# Rule of thumb: if a file is produced BY the build, it must be listed here --
# otherwise a stale copy left over from the old dev.sh flow silently becomes a
# build input.

# --- VCS / editor ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitmodules
.github
*.swp
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- dependencies (installed inside the build) ---
node_modules/

# --- outputs the old dev.sh extracted back onto the host ---
build/
hf/build/
assets/
assets_src/
base/**/*.pk3
base/hf/games.log
base/hf/q3config_server.cfg
html/hf/shenanigans/
# Tracked, but the web image takes the client from quake-build instead so the
# image always matches the current submodule.
html/ioquake3.js

# --- ioq3: the whole submodule is copied into the build, so exclude only what
#     must not come along.
#
#     node_modules is critical: the build stage installs ws@0.4.29 into
#     /opt/ioq3/node_modules before copying the tree, and the copy merges into
#     that directory -- a stray local ioq3/node_modules would clobber it.
#
#     misc/ is NOT excluded. It is only referenced by the Makefile's installer
#     and clean targets, so trimming it would be safe, but predicting which
#     non-code paths the build needs is exactly what broke the client compile on
#     ui/menudef.h. A few MB of context is cheaper than that class of bug. ---
ioq3/build/
ioq3/node_modules/
ioq3/.git

# --- compose and docs are never build inputs ---
compose.yml
compose.dev.yml
README.md
CONTAINERS.md
.mocharc.json
